body:
Reading the code paths:

- `ReqExclBulkScorer#score(LeafCollector, Bits, int, int)` its possible that `max == NO_MORE_DOCS` if that leaf slice is the entire leaf. In this case, I expect that it is as it threw on a cfs file.
- It seems possible that within `MaxScoreBulkScorer#score(LeafCollector, Bits, int, int)` that we actually iterate and force `outerWindowMax` to be NO_MORE_DOCS, just like the passed in `max`
- Then we come to `MaxScoreBulkScorer#scoreInnerWindowWithFilter(LeafCollector, Bits, int, DisiWrapper)` with the `max==NO_MORE_DOCS`. 


This is where I get stuck, I just don't see how `doc == NO_MORE_DOCS`. Here is the simplified loops (removing paths we don't hit in this stack trace).

```
private void scoreInnerWindowWithFilter(LeafCollector collector, Bits acceptDocs, int max, DisiWrapper filter) throws IOException {
    DisiWrapper top = essentialQueue.top();
    if (top.doc < filter.doc) {
      top.doc = top.approximation.advance(filter.doc);
    }

    int innerWindowMin = top.doc;
    // if `max` == NO_MORE_DOCS, the worst this can be is `NO_MORE_DOCS`
    int innerWindowMax = (int) Math.min(max, (long) innerWindowMin + INNER_WINDOW_SIZE);

    // SEEMS TO PROTECT AGAINST NO_MORE_DOCS???
    while (top.doc < innerWindowMax) {
      if (filter.doc < top.doc) {
        filter.doc = filter.approximation.advance(top.doc);
      }

      if (filter.doc != top.doc) {
        do {
          top.doc = top.iterator.advance(filter.doc);
          top = essentialQueue.updateTop();
        } while (top.doc < filter.doc);
      } else {
        int doc = top.doc;
        boolean match =
            (acceptDocs == null || acceptDocs.get(doc))
                && (filter.twoPhaseView == null || filter.twoPhaseView.matches());
        double score = 0;
        do {
          if (match) {
            score += top.scorer.score();
          }
          top.doc = top.iterator.nextDoc();
          top = essentialQueue.updateTop();
        } while (top.doc == doc);

        if (match) {
          scoreNonEssentialClauses(collector, doc, score, firstEssentialScorer);
        }
      }
    }
  }
```

If we get to `scoreNonEssentialClauses` where `doc==NO_MORE_DOCS` then it explains the EOF.

As this is the advance and score code `TermScorer` which calls `Lucene90NormsProducer#advancedExact`

```
  @Override
  public float score() throws IOException {
    var postingsEnum = this.postingsEnum;
    var norms = this.norms;

    long norm = 1L;
    if (norms != null && norms.advanceExact(postingsEnum.docID())) {
      norm = norms.longValue();
    }
    return scorer.score(postingsEnum.freq(), norm);
  }
```

